-- chem/fold.cub — the fold as a fiber (docs/chemical-identity.md, section X). One carrier at every
-- scale, written once over the element type so that each scale is data and not code (Avik,
-- 2026-11-18: "code should be absolutely minimal"; `factoring`): a type of elements, a label on
-- each, a relation on each ordered pair, and the arrangement at each element as a Cyc. Atoms with
-- their elements and bonds, residues with their kinds and contacts, secondary-structure elements with
-- theirs, are instances of one type, and a theorem proved here holds at every scale.
--   Arr            the carrier; Stereo's shape with the label and the pair relation as parameters.
--   cyc-rev        reflection of an arrangement, the cyclic order read the other way; one inverse
--                  rotation carries it along the rotation paths, so it is a function of the
--                  configuration and not of a drawing.
--   arr-mirror     the mirror image: every arrangement reflected, labels and pairs untouched.
--   arr-mirror-pairs  the mirror's pair relation is the original's, for every carrier at every
--                  scale: a bond graph or a contact map cannot tell a carrier from its mirror image.
--   bab            a beta-alpha-beta unit, the fold-scale instance; bab-contacts-same and
--                  bab-mirror-differs are the two halves of contact-map-mirror on it: same contacts,
--                  different arrangement (Richardson 1976: 83 of 85 crossovers right-handed), so the
--                  handedness is data the contact map does not hold.
--   transport-pairs, transport-pairs-sound  template transport along an alignment: a pair the
--                  alignment identifies takes the template's value, any other pair stays open, and
--                  the soundness of the first is a path.
import "identity.cub"

